 "_about": "Measured on the v2 Act 1 plates (public/img/v2) by scripts/images/measure-v2.py. Pixel coordinates in each plate (origin top-left). Quads are [topLeft, topRight, bottomRight, bottomLeft]. \"window\" is the glowing opening of the lens, out to the outer edge of its thin black border (sharp corners; the border's rounding is ignored); \"active\" is the 96 x 64 LCD area inside it, placed by the design's margins: pin the LCD there. cornerPinUV is the same divided by the plate size, for @remotion/effects cornerPin. On v2-p2-macro the keys are estimates (source field): only the top row shows, at the bottom edge. Keys: 1-9, star, 0, hash. homographyMmToPx maps the design (mm, research-v2/10-act1-phone-front.svg) to the plate. lightPass is the lit edit of the same plate (lit minus unlit = the light).",
